hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1162","Muhammad bin Yahya and Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr told us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Muammar told us, Muhammad said: On the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, secluded himself peace be upon him in the mosque, and he heard them reciting the recitation aloud. Abdul Rahman added: while he was in his dome, and they said: Then he revealed the curtains, and said: “Isn’t “All of you are communing with your Lord, so do not annoy one another, and do not raise one another’s reading above others.” Muhammad said: “Or in prayer.”"
